# Docker reads this, not .gitignore. One per site, because each site's build
# context is its own directory now rather than the repo root. Without it the frontend stage copies
# node_modules from the host into the build, which is slow and pointless since
# the image installs its own from the lockfile.
**/node_modules
**/build
**/bin
# Compiled inside the build stage; shipping the host's copy in would only
# slow the context transfer.
**/pdfs
**/og
# Runtime state. The GeoIP mmdb alone is 131MB, and sending it in the build
# context would dominate every single build.
**/data
# Generated in its own build stage from Natural Earth.
**/static_maps
# Generated inside the build from frontend/images/. Excluding it stops the
# later COPY of the whole frontend directory clobbering what was just built.
**/frontend/public/images
.git
.playwright-cli
**/.env
**/*.pem
